<%!-- The screen has two states, and the browser swaps between them (app.js,
      [data-pin-live] / [data-pin-expired]) when the PIN's window closes. Both
      are rendered here so the whole page is one server render: a member with no
      JavaScript keeps the live half and its plain "valid for 30 minutes"
      sentence, which is exactly what this page said nothing about until now.

      The swap spans the hero as well as the card, which is why the markers are
      a pair of plain attributes rather than one wrapper: leaving "Please check
      your INBOX." beside a card announcing that the PIN is dead is a page
      arguing with itself. Each state keeps the split the live one already had,
      the hero saying what the situation is and the card what to do about it, so
      neither sentence is written twice.

      Hiding the LIVE half is the point of the swap, not a nicety. All three
      controls in it are dead by then: the PIN can no longer verify, "Resend
      PIN" reads its address from the same cookie that has just expired, and
      "Cancel registration" would send somebody with no account yet to the login
      form. A screen full of controls that quietly do nothing is what made this
      read as the site being broken. --%>
<.auth_layout title={gettext("Please check your INBOX.")}>
  <:headline>
    <div data-pin-live>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold leading-tight md:text-3xl">
        {gettext("Please check your INBOX.")}
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-sm text-base leading-relaxed text-brand-50">
        {gettext("Your account has been created, and an email with a PIN has been sent. No passwords to remember! Once you enter your PIN below, you'll be logged in on this device for the next 90 days, or until you log out.")}
      </p>
    </div>

    <%!-- Plain `hidden`, and deliberately no display utility on this element or
          the one above: two classes that both set `display` is the issue #880
          trap, where the one Tailwind emits later silently wins.

          `tabindex="-1"` is here so app.js can move focus onto the panel when it
          takes over. A screen-reader user is mid-form when the field
          disappears, and an `aria-live` region announces content changes, not a
          sibling quietly being hidden. --%>
    <div data-pin-expired hidden tabindex="-1" class="focus:outline-none">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold leading-tight md:text-3xl">
        {gettext("The PIN has expired.")}
      </h1>
      <%!-- The deletion is real and it is close, so it is said plainly rather
            than softened away. The figure comes from the sweeper's own
            constants (Accounts.unconfirmed_registration_grace_minutes/0), and
            "about" is honest rather than vague: that job wakes every 15
            minutes, so no single minute is the truth. --%>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-sm text-base leading-relaxed text-brand-50">
        {ngettext(
          "Your sign-up was never confirmed, so we delete it automatically in about one minute.",
          "Your sign-up was never confirmed, so we delete it automatically in about %{count} minutes.",
          Vutuv.Accounts.unconfirmed_registration_grace_minutes()
        )}
      </p>
    </div>
  </:headline>

  <div data-pin-live>
    <%!-- "Enter your PIN" alone can be read as an instruction to invent one, and
          somebody who skims this page sees little else. The heading now says
          where the PIN comes from, and the placeholder says what it looks like,
          so the two lines answer different questions instead of repeating one. --%>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
      {gettext("Enter the PIN from the email")}
    </h2>

    <.form :let={f} for={%{}} action={~p"/login"} as={:session} class="mt-5 space-y-4" id="pin-form" method="post">
      <%!-- Greet first-time members as new, not with "Welcome back!". --%>
      <%= hidden_input f, :context, value: "registration" %>
      <%= text_input f, :pin, class: input_class(), autofocus: true, autocomplete: "one-time-code", inputmode: "numeric", placeholder: gettext("6-digit PIN"), "aria-describedby": "pin-time-left" %>
      <.button type="submit" class="w-full">{gettext("submit")}</.button>
    </.form>

    <.pin_time_left expires_at={@pin_expires_at} />

    <.pin_actions email={@pending_email} context={@pin_flow} />

    <.dev_mailbox_link />
  </div>

  <%!-- The way out, and better news than the hero above it: an abandoned
        sign-up is handed a fresh PIN when the same address comes back
        (Accounts.notify_registration_attempt/3), so nobody has to sit out the
        deletion first. --%>
  <div data-pin-expired hidden>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
      {gettext(
        "You can sign up again right away with the same email address, and we will send you a new PIN."
      )}
    </p>

    <.button href={~p"/"} class="mt-5 w-full">{gettext("Register again")}</.button>
  </div>
</.auth_layout>
